<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Send them in,\'94 Sarah said, heavy with sufferance. She had a question to settle.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Barely inside, Kleo blurted, \'93Are we too late?\'94\'97derailing Sarah\'92s resolutions.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah rose, readjusted her dress. \'93Too late for what?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo broke from the queue behind Kleo, strode over and, to Kathy\'92s horror, placed a proprietary hand on Sarah\'92s belly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ew!\'94 Kathy slapped him back.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo sighed with relief. \'93She\'92s still with child.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Of course she is,\'94 Kathy said, squeezing Sarah\'92s hand. \'93It\'92s not two months yet.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Forgive us,\'94 Kleo said. \'93The Travelator\'92s been especially\'85\'94 He squinted for words.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo offered, \'93It\'92s the Curse.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah and Kathy wore matching frowns. Everyone knew the Travelator, like all great public infrastructure, was so unpredictable no one used it, except squatters and necromancers. \'93The Travelator is cursed?\'94 Kathy\'92s voice dripped scepticism.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo rolled his eyes. \'93No, its propulsion. Curse! Q\'85E\'85R\'85S\'85E. Quantum Entanglement Rotary Steam Engine.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo shook his head. \'93Worst bit of tech since nuclear fission.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93As usual, it went to tender, cheapest bid won,\'94 Solo concluded.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo, already disinterested, sought the safety of examining his shoes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy massaged her temples. \'93You three should come with warning stickers.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah pounded her thighs in frustration. \'93Shut up! All of you. Just shut up.\'94 She skewered Kleo with a stare. \'93Which one of you taxers raped me?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Captain Denver A. Elvis, by the door, flipped open his police notebook. \'93Yeah, who\'92s the Holy Poppa?\'94 he asked, pencil poised. Outside, thousands of Elvi were already speculating.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo coughed into his fist. Solo side-eyed Chilo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You,\'94 Sarah accused Chilo, wielding the kind of horror reserved for discovering a hairball in your soup.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Immaculate conception?\'94 Chilo stammered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah flared. \'93What the tax?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo shrugged. \'93I thought it was immaculate, if I may say so myself. It wasn\'92t rape\'97I swear!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Are you claiming I consented?\'94 Sarah thundered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93N-n-no\'97I mean\'97\'94 (Let\'92s spare the page count: his stuttering could fill a novella.)\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It was a perfectly benign medical procedure,\'94 Solo insisted, all anxious diplomacy. \'93Foetal implanting.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I said we shouldn\'92t force you,\'94 Kleo offered, \'93I practically forbade it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Practically?\'94 Sarah shot back. \'93You 
\f2\i practically
\f1\i0  failed, then.\'94 She fumed, and Kathy feared a punch-up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo shrank.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah, finally, cooled herself enough to speak. \'93I\'92m not keeping it.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Keeping what?\'94 Solo blinked, searching the room for an unclaimed object.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93The baby.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The room chilled. Captain Denver holstered his notebook and slipped out.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo mustered himself. \'93But\'85 the exultation of science, the reunification of reason and art is at hand\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It is the end of days!\'94 Chilo proclaimed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo pulled a sanguine expression around his craggy face, and smiled while he kicked Chilo\'92s shin. \'93Shut up,\'94 he muttered wearily. \'93You\'92re scaring the foetus.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Oh, yes, I recall now,\'94 Sarah mocked. \'93I have a baby that will end the universe.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Ignore Chilo,\'94 Kleo counselled. \'93My esteemed colleague is mistaken. He\'92s merely referencing an aberrant misinterpretation of the prophecies.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Which is why there\'92s nothing to worry about,\'94 Solo said. \'93Your baby will be born almost entirely normally, and will have nothing to do with any of that apocalyptic nonsense you hear spread around.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Oh, give me strength,\'94 Kleo swore.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What apocalyptic nonsense?\'94 Sarah pressed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo stepped sideways, out of range of Kleo\'92s boot. \'93The coming of the One After the One ushers in the evacuation of this universe, and in its final, gasping picoseconds, the One After the One will ascend\'85\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Solo, seeing the pitch rise, cut in: \'93\'97and create a universe with a vastly improved user experience.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And all conspiracy theorists will be put to death,\'94 Chilo crowed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93By which he means, banned from social networks,\'94 Kleo clarified.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92d like to see how that works,\'94 Kathy drawled.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And the greedy shall get death by stadium meat pie,\'94 Chilo added.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo finally snapped. \'93Shut up, you two!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo kept ranting: \'93And there will only ever be one Elvis!\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You idiot, Chilo,\'94 Kleo said, glancing at the stuffed room. \'93Have you looked where you are? Who you\'92re surrounded by?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93You\'92re all idiots,\'94 Sarah erupted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>By this time Captain Denver was forgetting his stoic role as Sarah\'92s bodyguard/jailer and was foaming for a fight. He almost snapped his pencil.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Steady Cap\'92n Crunch,\'94 Sarah said, warding Captain Denver back to his station with an authoritative wave of her hand.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos shrugged his anger off and began again with a forced measure of pace. \'93What 
